{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Is it a small thing that you have taken, etc.</b> Leah's intent follows the approach of Amram, of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 72), that Jacob's fixed bed was with Rachel. Therefore she said, ״הַמְעַט קַחְתֵּךְ אֶת אִישִׁי״ — meaning: the extra portion that is with you is subtracted from Leah's portion. And her saying <b>and you shall take</b>, etc., intends to say that the dimension of conception comes about through much coupling and the continuous lying with the husband, as the Sages of blessed memory stated (Ḥullin 11b) in several places, and the action of the mandrakes is a segullah for conception (Zohar 1:157a). Therefore she said: the continuous taking of my husband to yourself, as mentioned, should suffice for you — so why do you add the taking of my son's mandrakes?" "<b>And the reason</b> that Jacob would make a distinction between his two wives is that he was under no obligation to Leah other than the conjugal duty mentioned in the Torah (Exodus 21:10): ״לֹא יִגְרָע״, for he did not marry her with his will and knowledge, as indeed was the case — unlike Rachel, who was his wife and for her he had served both the first time and the second." "<b>Therefore he shall lie with you, etc.</b> It would appear that the matter depended on Rachel's consent, and she says <b>therefore</b> — meaning, on account of your giving me mandrakes, etc.:" "<b>Or</b> it may intend the language of an oath, since these are matters that cannot be acquired except through an oath, because [Leah] did not transfer to her anything of substance. And see what I have written on the verse (Genesis 25:33) ״הִשָּׁבְעָה לִי״ regarding the sale of Esau's birthright."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:06.254023403Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}